<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0044326> rdfs:label "developmental delay and seizures with or without movement abnormalities" ;
    dcterms:description "DEDSM is a neurodevelopmental disorder characterized by global developmental delay, variable intellectual disability, and early-onset seizures with a myoclonic component. Most patients have delayed motor development and show abnormal movements, including ataxia, dystonia, and tremor (summary by {1:Hamdan et al., 2017})." ;
